Upholstery cleaning is a lane I’ve lived in for years. From high-end leather lounges to family couches that have absorbed a decade of life, pets, spills, and sun.
</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl uppercase text-[var(--primary)] mt-12 mb-4">
Physics vs Marketing
</h2>

<p>
Most people expect a miracle. What we actually deliver is a technical reset. Over time, furniture fibres bind with oils, skin cells, dust mites, and airborne contaminants. These aren’t surface issues. They’re embedded.
</p>

<p class="mt-4">
When I carry out <a href="upholstery-cleaning.html" class="font-bold text-[var(--primary)] underline">professional upholstery cleaning in Hervey Bay</a>, my focus is hygiene and longevity. I remove what’s *in* the fabric. I cannot undo damage *to* the fabric.
</p>

<blockquote class="my-12 p-6 bg-white/40 rounded-xl border-l-4 border-[var(--primary)] italic">
“I won’t charge you to attempt the impossible. Sun fade, fibre wear, and dye loss aren’t dirt.”
</blockquote>

<h2 class="text-2xl uppercase text-[var(--primary)] mt-12 mb-4">
What Professional Cleaning Actually Involves
</h2>

<p>
This isn’t a spray-and-suck job. We use controlled chemistry, heat, dwell time, and extraction to safely remove contaminants without weakening fibres.
</p>

<ul class="mt-6 space-y-3">
  <li><strong>Deep soil removal:</strong> eliminating abrasive grit that shortens fabric life</li>
  <li><strong>Odour neutralisation:</strong> removing bacteria rather than masking smells</li>
</ul>

<h2 class="text-2xl uppercase text-red-600 mt-12 mb-4">
What Can’t Be Fixed
</h2>

<p>
Some damage is permanent. No honest technician will tell you otherwise.
</p>

<ul class="mt-6 space-y-3">
  <li>✕ Fibre wear and thinning</li>
  <li>✕ Permanent dye transfer</li>
  <li>✕ Chemical burns from DIY products</li>
</ul>

<h2 class="text-2xl uppercase text-[var(--primary)] mt-12 mb-4">
Final Word
</h2>

<p>
Your furniture is one of the most-used items in your home. It deserves proper care, not rushed jobs or false promises.
</p>

<p class="font-bold italic mt-4">
If it can be saved, I’ll save it. If it can’t, I’ll tell you before unloading the van.
